module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularSequence.KoszulIdealOpenSubspace
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.BaseIdealMultiple

/-!
# A sheaf of ideals generated over an open, read on the slice site

Let `X` be a ringed space, `𝓘 ⊆ O_X` a sheaf of ideals and `f₁, …, f_r` sections of `O_X` over an
open `U` generating `𝓘` there in the sense of [Stacks, Tag 063D]: the sections of `𝓘` over every
`V ⊆ U` are those of the sheaf of ideals the `fᵢ` generate.  The gluing of the local statements of
[Stacks, Tag 0BQY] runs on the slice site `Opens X / U`, and what it consumes there is that two
sheaves of ideals of the slice structure sheaf agree: the local closure of the objectwise span of
the restrictions of the `fᵢ`, and the local closure of the objectwise image of the inclusion of
`𝓘`.  This file proves that they do.

Both are local closures on the *same* site, so what separates them is not a change of site but
the two descriptions of the ideal the `fᵢ` generate: an infimum of subsheaves on `Opens X`, and a
local closure of an objectwise span on `Opens X / U`.  The meeting point is the germ criterion
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.mem_generatedIdealOn_iff`, from which a section of the
generated ideal over `V ⊆ U` is, near each point of `V`, an `O_X`-combination of the `fᵢ`; that
local representation is what the covering sieve witnessing membership in the local closure is
built from.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.exists_res_eq_sum_of_mem_generatedIdealOn`: **the
  local representation.**  A section of the ideal generated by `f₁, …, f_r` over `V ⊆ U` agrees,
  on a neighbourhood of each point of `V`, with an `O_X`-combination of the restrictions of the
  `fᵢ`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.sliceIdealOfSections_eq_idealOfHom`: **the two
  sheaves of ideals on the slice site agree**, and
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.sectionIdeal_sliceIdealOfSections_eq`: their
  sections agree over every object — the form the gluing consumes.

## Implementation notes

The local representation is stated with the restriction maps written out rather than as membership
in a submodule: the covering sieve it feeds is a sieve on an object of `Opens X / U`, where
membership is membership in the objectwise span, and the span's description
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.mem_spanSections_obj` is itself a combination with explicit coefficients.

Equality of the two local closures is proved by antisymmetry from
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.localClosure_le`, which says that the local closure is the least submodule
of the *sheaf* above a submodule of its underlying presheaf; so each direction only has to place
one objectwise description inside the other's local closure.  In one direction that is immediate,
the restrictions of the `fᵢ` being sections of `𝓘`; the other direction is the local
representation.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BQY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BQY)
* [Stacks Project, Definition 31.21.2 (Tag 063D)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063D)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Sheaf Opposite TopologicalSpace
open AlgebraicGeometry RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction
open Stacks.RingTheory.QuasiRegular

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf

open Stacks.Sites Stacks.SheafOfModules
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasiRegular
open Stacks.RingedSpace

variable {X : RingedSpace.{u, u}} (U : Opens X.carrier)
  {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → X.presheaf.obj (op U))

/-! ### The local representation of a section of the generated ideal -/

/-- **A section of the ideal generated by `f₁, …, f_r` over `U` is locally a combination of
them.**  Over a subopen `V` of `U`, a section of `generatedIdealOn X U f` agrees on some
neighbourhood of each point of `V` with an `O_X`-combination of the restrictions of the `fᵢ`.

The germ criterion `mem_generatedIdealOn_iff` turns membership into membership of each germ in the
ideal the germs of the `fᵢ` generate; the coefficients of one such germ combination are realised
by sections over a single neighbourhood
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasiRegular.exists_nhds_germ_eq`), after which the difference of the
two sides has vanishing germ and so vanishes on a smaller neighbourhood
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasiRegular.exists_nhds_eq_zero_of_germ_eq_zero`). -/
theorem exists_res_eq_sum_of_mem_generatedIdealOn (V : Opens X.carrier) (hVU : V ≤ U)
    (s : X.presheaf.obj (op V)) (hs : s ∈ (generatedIdealOn X U f).obj (op V))
    (y : X.carrier) (hy : y ∈ V) :
    ∃ (W : Opens X.carrier) (hWV : W ≤ V), y ∈ W ∧
      ∃ a : Fin r → X.presheaf.obj (op W),
        X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWV).op s
          = ∑ k, a k * X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hWV.trans hVU)).op (f k) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨cc, hcc⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_range_iff_exists_fun.mp
    (germ_mem_of_mem_generatedIdealOn U f V s hs y hy (hVU hy))
  obtain ⟨V₀, hyV₀, b, hb⟩ := exists_nhds_germ_eq (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin r)) y cc
  have hyW₀ : y ∈ V ⊓ V₀ := ⟨hy, hyV₀⟩
  have hinfU : V ⊓ V₀ ≤ U := le_trans (inf_le_left (a := V) (b := V₀)) hVU
  set dd : X.presheaf.obj (op (V ⊓ V₀)) :=
    X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (inf_le_left (a := V) (b := V₀))).op s
      - ∑ i, X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (inf_le_right (a := V) (b := V₀))).op (b i)
          * X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hinfU).op (f i) with hdd
  have hgerm : X.presheaf.germ (V ⊓ V₀) y hyW₀ dd = 0 := by
    rw [hdd, map_sub, map_sum, sub_eq_zero,
      TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply X.presheaf
        (homOfLE (inf_le_left (a := V) (b := V₀))) y hyW₀ s, ← hcc]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
    rw [map_mul,
      TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply X.presheaf (homOfLE hinfU) y hyW₀ (f i),
      TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply X.presheaf
        (homOfLE (inf_le_right (a := V) (b := V₀))) y hyW₀ (b i),
      hb i (Finset.mem_univ i)]
    rfl
  obtain ⟨W, hyW, hWW₀, hdW⟩ :=
    exists_nhds_eq_zero_of_germ_eq_zero (V ⊓ V₀) dd y hyW₀ hgerm
  refine ⟨W, hWW₀.trans (inf_le_left (a := V) (b := V₀)), hyW,
    fun i => X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hWW₀.trans (inf_le_right (a := V) (b := V₀)))).op (b i), ?_⟩
  rw [hdd, map_sub, map_sum, sub_eq_zero] at hdW
  rw [← Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasiRegular.res_res
    (inf_le_left (a := V) (b := V₀)) hWW₀ s, hdW]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
  rw [map_mul, Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasiRegular.res_res,
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasiRegular.res_res]

/-! ### The two sheaves of ideals on the slice site -/

variable (J : (structureSheafModule X).Submodule)

/-- **The sheaf of ideals of the slice structure sheaf generated by the inclusion of `𝓘`.**  The
restriction to the slice site over `U` of the inclusion of a sheaf of ideals of `O_X` is a
morphism into the slice structure sheaf, and this is the sheaf of ideals it generates there.

The ascription is the point: the inclusion is a morphism of sheaves of modules over the structure
sheaf of rings at the `AlgebraicGeometry.structureSheafRing` spelling, which is
the spelling `Stacks.SheafOfModules.sliceRingSheaf` is the slice of. -/
abbrev sliceIdealOfInclusion : Stacks.Sites.IdealSubsheaf.{u, u, u} (X.sheaf.over U) :=
  idealOfHom (O := X.sheaf.over U)
    ((_root_.SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (structureSheafRing X) U).map J.ι)

/-- **The sections of the slice reading of `𝓘` are the sections of `𝓘` over the underlying
open.**  The restriction to the slice site is a pushforward along `Over.forget U`, so the
objectwise image of the inclusion of `𝓘` over a slice object is the image of the inclusion over
its underlying open, which is `𝓘` there. -/
theorem mem_of_mem_presheafRangeSubmodule_overFunctor_ι (W : (Over U)ᵒᵖ)
    (x : (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit (sliceRingSheaf U)).val.obj W)
    (hx : x ∈ (presheafRangeSubmodule
      ((_root_.SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} (structureSheafRing X) U).map J.ι).val).obj W) :
    x ∈ J.obj (op W.unop.left) := by
  obtain ⟨m, rfl⟩ := hx
  exact m.2

/-- **The restrictions of `f₁, …, f_r` to a slice object are sections of `𝓘` there.**  Each `fᵢ`
is a section of `𝓘` over `U` — that is the generation hypothesis read at `U` itself — and a sheaf
of ideals is stable under restriction. -/
theorem map_mem_of_isGeneratedByOn (hJ : IsGeneratedByOn X J U f) (W : (Over U)ᵒᵖ) (k : Fin r) :
    X.presheaf.map W.unop.hom.op (f k) ∈ J.obj (op W.unop.left) :=
  J.toSubmodule.map_mem W.unop.hom.op (by rw [hJ U le_rfl]; exact mem_generatedIdealOn X U f k)

/-- **The sheaf of ideals the sections `f₁, …, f_r` generate on the slice site over `U` is the one
the inclusion of `𝓘` generates there.**  This is the hypothesis `hgen` of the gluing of
[Stacks, Tag 0BQY], discharged from the tag's own generation hypothesis.

Both sides are local closures of submodules of the underlying presheaf of the slice structure
sheaf, and `Stacks.SheafOfModules.localClosure_le` makes the local closure the least submodule of
the sheaf above such a submodule, so it is enough to place each description inside the other's
local closure.  One direction is `map_mem_of_isGeneratedByOn`: the restrictions of the `fᵢ` are
sections of `𝓘`, hence so is every combination of them.  The other is the local representation
`exists_res_eq_sum_of_mem_generatedIdealOn`: a section of `𝓘` over the underlying open of a slice
object is, near each of its points, a combination of the restrictions of the `fᵢ`, and those
neighbourhoods form a covering sieve of that object. -/
theorem sliceIdealOfSections_eq_idealOfHom (hJ : IsGeneratedByOn X J U f) :
    sliceIdealOfSections U f = sliceIdealOfInclusion U J := by
  refine le_antisymm (localClosure_le fun W x hx => ?_) (localClosure_le fun W x hx => ?_)
  · obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := (mem_spanSections_obj _ _ W x).mp hx
    refine Submodule.sum_mem _ fun k _ => Submodule.smul_mem _ _ ?_
    exact le_localClosure _ W ⟨⟨_, map_mem_of_isGeneratedByOn U f J hJ W k.down⟩, rfl⟩
  · have hxJ : x ∈ (generatedIdealOn X U f).obj (op W.unop.left) := by
      rw [← hJ W.unop.left (leOfHom W.unop.hom)]
      exact mem_of_mem_presheafRangeSubmodule_overFunctor_ι U J W x hx
    change x ∈ (localClosure (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit (sliceRingSheaf U))
      (spanSections (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit (sliceRingSheaf U)).val
        (sliceSections U f))).obj W
    rw [mem_localClosure_obj, GrothendieckTopology.mem_over_iff,
      Opens.mem_grothendieckTopology]
    intro y hy
    obtain ⟨W', hW'V, hyW', a, ha⟩ := exists_res_eq_sum_of_mem_generatedIdealOn U f
      W.unop.left (leOfHom W.unop.hom) x hxJ y hy
    refine ⟨W', homOfLE hW'V, ?_, hyW'⟩
    rw [Sieve.overEquiv_iff]
    refine (mem_spanSections_obj (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit (sliceRingSheaf U)).val
      (sliceSections U f) _ _).mpr ⟨fun k => a k.down, Eq.trans ?_ ha.symm⟩
    exact Fintype.sum_equiv Equiv.ulift _ _ fun _ => rfl

/-- **The sections of the two sheaves of ideals agree over every object of `Opens X / U`.**  This
is `sliceIdealOfSections_eq_idealOfHom` read on sections, which is the shape the chain of
presentations of [Stacks, Tag 0BQY] consumes. -/
theorem sectionIdeal_sliceIdealOfSections_eq (hJ : IsGeneratedByOn X J U f) (W : (Over U)ᵒᵖ) :
    sectionIdeal (sliceIdealOfSections U f) W = sectionIdeal (sliceIdealOfInclusion U J) W :=
  congrArg (fun I => sectionIdeal I W) (sliceIdealOfSections_eq_idealOfHom U f J hJ)

/-! ### The slice reading of a sheaf of ideals -/

/-- **A sheaf of ideals of `O_X`, read on the slice site over `U`**: over an object of
`Opens X / U` its sections are the sections of the sheaf of ideals over the underlying open.

That this is again a sheaf of ideals, and not merely a submodule of the underlying presheaf, is
because the covering sieves of the slice site are the covering sieves of the underlying open read
back along `Over.forget U` (`CategoryTheory.Sieve.overEquiv_iff`), so the locality condition at a
slice object is the locality condition of the sheaf of ideals at its underlying open. -/
def overIdealSubsheaf : Stacks.Sites.IdealSubsheaf.{u, u, u} (X.sheaf.over U) where
  obj W := J.obj (op W.unop.left)
  map {_ _} g _ hx := J.toSubmodule.map_mem g.unop.left.op hx
  isSheaf {W} s hs := by
    refine J.isSheaf (X := op W.unop.left) s
      ((Opens.mem_grothendieckTopology _).mpr fun y hy => ?_)
    obtain ⟨V, g, hg, hyV⟩ := (Opens.mem_grothendieckTopology _).mp hs y hy
    exact ⟨V, g, (Sieve.overEquiv_iff _ _).mp hg, hyV⟩

/-- **The sheaf of ideals the inclusion generates on the slice site is the slice reading of the
sheaf of ideals.**  The objectwise image of the restricted inclusion is already the sheaf of
ideals read on slice objects, and the slice reading is already a sheaf of ideals, so the local
closure adds nothing. -/
theorem sliceIdealOfInclusion_eq_overIdealSubsheaf :
    sliceIdealOfInclusion U J = overIdealSubsheaf U J :=
  le_antisymm
    (localClosure_le fun W x hx =>
      mem_of_mem_presheafRangeSubmodule_overFunctor_ι U J W x hx)
    (fun W _ hx => le_localClosure _ W ⟨⟨_, hx⟩, rfl⟩)

/-- **The sheaf of ideals the sections `f₁, …, f_r` generate on the slice site over `U` is the
slice reading of the sheaf of ideals they generate.**  This is
`sliceIdealOfSections_eq_idealOfHom` with the local closure of the image removed. -/
theorem sliceIdealOfSections_eq_overIdealSubsheaf (hJ : IsGeneratedByOn X J U f) :
    sliceIdealOfSections U f = overIdealSubsheaf U J :=
  (sliceIdealOfSections_eq_idealOfHom U f J hJ).trans
    (sliceIdealOfInclusion_eq_overIdealSubsheaf U J)

/-- **The sections over a slice object of the sheaf of ideals the `fᵢ` generate are the sections
of the sheaf of ideals over the underlying open.**  This is the form in which the recognition of
the quotient of the slice structure sheaf consumes the generation hypothesis: what it asks is
that the kernel of the restricted quotient map agree, over every slice object, with these
sections. -/
theorem sectionIdeal_sliceIdealOfSections_eq_obj (hJ : IsGeneratedByOn X J U f)
    (W : (Over U)ᵒᵖ) :
    sectionIdeal (sliceIdealOfSections U f) W = J.obj (op W.unop.left) := by
  rw [sliceIdealOfSections_eq_overIdealSubsheaf U f J hJ]
  rfl

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf

end
